## Adding an issue to the board

```bash
gh project item-add {{ board_number }} --owner {{ board_owner }} --url <ISSUE_URL>
```

After adding, run `n3rv board sync --issue <N> --phase todo` to set the
initial state.

## Workflow: after an SDD phase completes

After `memory_save` succeeds in any SDD phase skill:

1. Run `n3rv board sync --issue <N> --phase <phase>`.
2. If it exits `3`, the issue is not on the board: add it with
   `gh project item-add` and rerun. Report the failure — do not swallow it.
3. If it exits `2`, the board has duplicate items for that issue: stop and
   report both item ids.

## Rules

- NEVER update the board before the memory_save succeeds. The board is downstream of MAGI.
- Always update Status AND SDD Phase together — `n3rv board sync` does this in one mutation.
- Never skip an absent item silently; exit code `3` is a finding to report.
- All commands use `--owner {{ board_owner }}`, never `--org`.
